---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import RegisterStructureDemo from "../../components/RegisterStructureDemo.astro";
import StructureFacts from "../../components/StructureFacts.astro";
import TermCallout from "../../components/TermCallout.astro";
import { lwwRegisterTerm } from "../../lib/atlas/standalone-terms";
import "../../styles/set-lesson.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LWWRegister"
  description="Alice and Bob race trail-status reports, and timestamp metadata selects one winner."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="LWWRegister"
>
  <article class="register-lesson">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structures</p>
      <h1>LWWRegister</h1>
      <p class="structure-summary">
        The ranger needs one trail status before the morning bulletin. Alice
        reports open while Bob reports closed. Carol may receive either report
        first, but every notebook must choose the same answer.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-lww-register" />
    </header>

    <StructureFacts
      family="CRDT"
      model="State-based last-writer-wins register"
      updates="String writes with an ordering value"
      merge="Keep the greatest timestamp; break ties by writer ID."
      delivery="Safe under repeated and out-of-order delivery"
      bestFor="One deterministic value when losing a concurrent write is acceptable"
      cost="One value, timestamp, and writer ID"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="clock-title">
      <h2 id="clock-title">The sequence number becomes the timestamp</h2>
      <p>
        A <dfn><a href="/glossary/#last-writer-wins-register">last-writer-wins register</a></dfn>
        {" "}does not use message arrival order. It compares the timestamp
        attached to each write. For these reports, the ranger's sequencer
        supplies that timestamp as a sequence number.
      </p>
      <TermCallout {...lwwRegisterTerm} />
      <figure>
        <table aria-label="LWWRegister timestamp race">
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Writer</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Sequence number</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Alice · A</th><td>Trail open</td><td>1</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Bob · B</th><td>Trail closed</td><td>2</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Winner</th><td>Trail closed</td><td>2 is greater</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <figcaption>Carol gets the same winner even if the network delivers Alice's report last.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        The sequence number acts as the timestamp and is the primary
        comparison. If two writes have the same timestamp, the greater writer
        ID breaks the tie. This fallback gives every notebook the same answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <RegisterStructureDemo
      kind="lww-register"
      title="Choose one field report"
      description="The ranger assigns Alice's report sequence 1 and Bob's report sequence 2. Later delivery cannot replace a greater sequence number."
      rule="Use the greatest sequence number."
      raceLabel="Sequence and share the reports"
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="limit-title">
      <h2 id="limit-title">The losing report disappears</h2>
      <p>
        The rule gives the ranger one answer, but it cannot show whether Alice
        and Bob disagreed. If both reports are valid evidence, choosing a winner
        is too destructive. The next register keeps both concurrent values.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title">Sources and implementation</h2>
      <p>
        The demo follows Watershed's{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/tylerbutler/watershed/blob/4a8739323ee491f353fcaa8ccfb0488419c1cd43/src/watershed/lww_register_kernel.gleam">LWWRegister kernel</a>
        {" "}and its timestamp-plus-author comparison rule.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="structure-next" aria-label="Continue through register structures">
      <a href="/structures/registers/">Back to register family</a>
      <a href="/structures/multi-value-register/">Continue to MvRegister</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
